he business a  lot of the times these athletes or  entertainers or whoever  kind of give a canned answer about what  the game was like well you know  we're taking it one play at a time we're  going to do this do that when they  answer  the definition of excellence they take  the time special care  and really give some interesting  different answers you know marcus allen  the  nfl hall of famer says excellence is a  culture  tiger woods when i asked him most  recently at the match in a press  conference i said tiger  how do you define excellence to him  excellence is winning  and there's so many different answers of  people that it just made it very  interesting and  seeing their reaction i think is what  truly motivated me  to do this podcast colbert has already  landed five of his first ten guests  and he's landing some very interesting  people votes which are greg maddox  his brother mike maddox susan anton bill  walton  and then napoleon mccallum u.s naval  graduate former oakland raider  and he's kind of truly the one final  person that inspired me  when i was wondering should i do this  when everybody's having so many  difficult times should we be talking  about excellence  he just kind of looked at me and said  you know brian any time to talk about  excellence is a great time to talk about  excellence so  you know i decided to do this and  talking to greg maddox he had some great  stories  inspired by a fortune cookie well yeah  there's a few they seem to pop up  anytime  the situation comes up you think of one  i mean there's tons of them  uh probably the one i probably use the  most was  i actually it on a fortune cookie it  said confucius once said  underestimating your opponent could lead  to catastrophe and then the performer  susan anton  just some great stories about uh  spending time with george burns kenny  rogers and i remember  the thrill of seeing sammy davis jr up  on the stage at the sands hotel  i was 16 years old i was able to get in  because i looked older  and he dazzled me and bill walton having  bill walton give me a 16 minute  definition of excellence with something  that i'll never forget and the  interesting thing is he wandered and  talked for 16 minutes about when i asked  him how do you define excellence  but the whole thing was perfectly tied  together because you'll never  learn what you don't want to know so  many of life  lessons it takes talent to get to the  top  takes character to stay there never  measure yourself by what you  haven't done but rather by what you  could have  or should have been able to do those who  are not willing to risk  going too far will never know how far  they can go this is about seeking out  and finding the excellence in the world  because it's out there and i think  hopefully especially during these times  to talk about excellence to be positive  and try to do good things when so many  people are struggling maybe in a small  way  you know we can give back and try to  make the world a little bit better place  if we can  well we're officially launched it's  xsleep.com xlete.com  all the podcasts and news about  excellence is on there we're currently  getting up on all the major podcast  networks but that takes a little bit of  time to get  uploaded and all that kind of stuff but  we're fully live you can listen to them  right now at xsleep.com  all right thank you very much brian we  appreciate that xsleet.com interesting  excellence all right we'll
 

